# New practical examples informed by the archived articles; outdated metrics and claims excluded.
EXTRAS={
20:[('Build one complete product before a catalogue','Start with a small deliverable you can open and test yourself. A PDF guide with a short readme is easier to troubleshoot than twenty unfinished products. Keep the editable source and a separate customer-ready export. Give the file a meaningful name; a buyer should not have to guess what final-v7-really-final.pdf contains. Prepare a sample that accurately represents the paid product, including its layout and depth.'),('Configure the Shopify product for digital delivery','Create the product with a specific title, price, cover and description. In its shipping settings, mark it as a digital rather than physical product so an unnecessary shipping charge is not introduced. Inventory is a separate decision: a repeatable file may not need stock tracking, but a limited commission or finite licence-key pool does. Do not disable stock safeguards indiscriminately. Save the product before connecting its delivery in BIG.'),('Choose the delivery mode that matches the promise','For a finished ebook, template or audio pack, choose standard delivery. Use custom products when work happens after purchase, such as an individual portrait. Use a scheduled product for a specific release date. In each case, attach the correct file, link or key and check the product or variant association. Describe any wait on the product page, not only in the confirmation email.'),('Run a real acceptance checklist','Complete a controlled test purchase using Shopify’s supported test procedure for your payment setup. Check the purchased variant, payment state, delivery email, post-purchase access and downloaded contents. Open the result on a phone as well as a computer. Repeat with a mixed cart if you sell physical items. Finally, check what happens when a buyer closes checkout and returns later. Keep the results so you can repeat the same checks after changing a file or theme.')],
19:[('Design the buyer’s first five minutes','A useful template pack begins with a specific task: a salon announcing available appointments, a freelancer preparing a proposal, or a teacher creating a lesson sheet. Use realistic placeholder copy so buyers understand what to replace. Make recurring elements consistent and avoid locking ordinary text fields unnecessarily. A smaller coordinated pack can be easier to use than a large collection with inconsistent spacing and fonts.'),('Package a link, not your working master','The practical handoff from the original guide is still valuable: create a short welcome PDF with the template link, three or four steps and a support contact. Generate the appropriate template-sharing link in Canva and verify that it creates a buyer’s copy instead of exposing your master for shared editing. Open it using a separate account. Check every promised page, font and export size rather than testing only the cover.'),('Make paid requirements visible before purchase','Check whether any assets or functions require Canva Pro. A buyer should not discover a paid requirement after paying you. Clearly label the account requirements and provide suitable alternatives where you can. Canva’s content licence and your product licence are separate: your terms cannot grant rights that you do not have. Link buyers to the relevant requirements rather than describing every Canva asset as unrestricted.'),('Use a support-ready product description','State the number of layouts, dimensions, editability, included formats and permitted uses. Show a close-up of an actual layout in addition to attractive mockups. Explain that delivery is digital, which file contains the link and how to contact you if access fails. For updates, decide whether the offer includes future versions and document that choice. Then test the welcome PDF through the full Shopify purchase flow.')],
15:[('Treat a key pool like inventory','Keep a secure original export and organise keys by product edition. Before launch, verify the required import format and reject empty lines or duplicate values in your source list. Use disposable test keys for setup. A reusable PDF and a unique activation code are different resources: the PDF can be delivered repeatedly while each code must follow your licensing rules. Plan replenishment before running a campaign.'),('Test two purchases, not just one','A single test can show that a code arrives, but not that the next customer receives a different appropriate code. Place controlled test orders for each relevant edition and quantity. Check the delivered key, product mapping and remaining inventory. Test the last available key and the exhausted state so you know how the store should behave. Do not assume a low-stock alert or an automatic stock block exists without verifying it in your setup.'),('Separate fulfilment from activation support','A delivery app gives a buyer the code. Your software or licensing provider determines whether it activates, on which devices and for how long. Document how support distinguishes a missing delivery from an invalid activation. If an order is refunded, decide what happens to that entitlement in the licensing system. Refunding a Shopify order should not be assumed to revoke an already delivered key automatically.')],
18:[('Name files around the buyer’s frame','The useful detail in the original guide was the handoff: a customer with a frame needs a recognisable size, not your internal artboard name. Package supported ratios and dimensions clearly, such as a 2:3 file and an A-series file. Add a short printing guide and say which sizes have been tested. Inspect the image at full size for scanning dust, compression artefacts and accidental crop marks before creating the customer download.'),('Offer licences buyers can understand','Separate a personal print licence from a commercial licence when the permitted uses differ. Explain the number or type of permitted uses, whether modification is allowed and whether redistribution of the source file is excluded. A higher-priced file is not automatically an exclusive licence. Put the important terms near the buying decision and include a copy in the delivered package.'),('Keep commissions out of the instant-download promise','For a custom portrait or illustration, collect the required brief and agree a clear turnaround. Define what a revision means and which final formats will be delivered. Use a custom product workflow so buyers understand they are waiting for completed work. Keep original, ready-made prints in standard delivery. Mixing the two without a timing explanation creates avoidable support requests.')],
21:[('Build a book package readers can navigate','Keep the main book easy to identify and separate optional worksheets or bonuses. Offer the formats you can support, for example a fixed-layout PDF and a reflowable EPUB. Include a short device guide instead of assuming everyone knows how to load an ebook into their reader. A sample chapter should demonstrate the actual writing and layout, not only a cover mockup. Test links, contents navigation and embedded fonts before uploading.'),('Compare channels using your actual audience','A direct store lets you shape the offer, bundle and checkout experience. It also means you are responsible for reaching readers. A marketplace can provide discovery, but discoverability is not a guaranteed sale. Compare net proceeds using the applicable fees, royalty terms, acquisition costs and content production costs. Do not decide using an invented universal profit margin or a promise that an app creates traffic.'),('Make exclusivity and updates explicit','Before selling the same ebook in two places, check whether the title is enrolled in an exclusive programme such as KDP Select. Keep a record of the relevant term dates. On your own product page, explain whether the purchase includes later editions or only the current version. That small distinction matters for manuals, reports and other books that can become outdated.')],
25:[('Package for the way musicians search and work','Use filenames that identify the pack, sound, tempo and key where those fields apply. Separate one-shots, loops and stems into meaningful groups rather than one unlabelled archive. Include a compact readme that explains sample rate, bit depth, included formats and installation steps if relevant. Test the extracted files on a clean machine; the fact that they play inside your production project is not sufficient.'),('Keep audio quality and licence tiers separate','An MP3, lossless master and multitrack stem package can serve different needs. Describe the format and the permitted use independently. A WAV file is not automatically an exclusive commercial licence. If you offer different tiers, map each Shopify product or variant to its actual package and test every option. Only sell music, recordings and samples you are authorised to distribute.'),('Calculate the transfer behind a launch','A 500 MB pack delivered 200 times is about 100 GB of transfer in decimal units, before retries or extra formats. The stored catalogue may still be only 500 MB. This is why a storage allowance and a bandwidth allowance cannot be compared as if they were the same number. Model a normal month and a release month, leave practical headroom and check actual usage after launch.')],
27:[('Create a start-here file that earns its place','A self-guided course needs an obvious first step. Put the lesson sequence, expected prerequisites and links to supporting exercises in one short contents file. Number lessons consistently and name worksheets after the lesson they support. Explain whether students should download everything or work lesson by lesson. This small amount of instructional design often matters more than adding another bonus file.'),('Choose delivery or an LMS deliberately','A downloadable workshop works when the buyer can learn independently from files. A programme that requires graded assignments, progress tracking or certificates needs additional systems. Keep that boundary visible in your sales page. If you use an external learning platform, verify its enrolment and access process; sending a link does not create an account or enforce paid access by itself.'),('Budget video before promising a large library','List the total size of the customer package and multiply it by likely downloads, including repeats. For illustration, a 2 GB workshop downloaded 300 times transfers about 600 GB. Compress thoughtfully and offer transcripts, but inspect legibility of on-screen details after export. Test on a slower connection and a phone. A fixed launch date is also different from individual weekly lesson unlocks after each purchase.')],
31:[('Make a release manifest','Record the product, edition, operating system, architecture, version and intended file for each sellable option. This can be a simple internal table. Keep the previous stable release available to your team and retain the source build separately from customer downloads. A clear manifest makes it much easier to notice that a Windows buyer has accidentally been mapped to a macOS archive.'),('Test beyond the download button','Use a clean supported environment to install the delivered file. If activation is required, test the delivered key against the expected edition. Verify that your installation guide explains the normal process and recognised publisher information. Do not tell customers to disable security protections as a standard installation step. Signing, application updates and activation enforcement remain your software distribution responsibilities.'),('Plan an update and rollback policy','Decide whether a purchase includes only the current major version, a defined update period or later releases. State this before purchase and test access for an existing customer when changing a file. Keep release notes and a recovery plan for a faulty build. A delivery problem and a software defect require different fixes, so gather the order reference and reproducible technical details without requesting unnecessary personal data.')],
33:[('Choose a deterrent that keeps the book readable','A watermark should support the product experience. Try the chosen stamp on a text-heavy page, a full-page image and a worksheet with writing space. Check contrast and margins in both a reader and a printed sample. Use only the buyer or order information appropriate for the purpose and explain the practice. More personal information does not automatically mean more effective protection.'),('Build a response plan for a suspected leak','Keep the original source, delivery settings and relevant order record so you can investigate accurately. A copied file or visible stamp is a signal, not conclusive proof of who shared it. Review the evidence and the platform’s reporting route before making an accusation. For legitimate customers, maintain a clear recovery process so protection settings do not turn a device change into a lost purchase.')],
34:[('Test the delivered file, not only the setting','Start from an unprotected PDF and keep a clean master copy. Enable the available stamping options in BIG, then use a controlled order to inspect the actual download. Test multiple layouts and confirm the intended buyer or order information appears. If a PDF is delivered inside a ZIP, do not assume the archive’s contents are stamped automatically. Check the current documentation for the supported packaging and download mode.'),('Separate samples from personalised purchases','For a preview, a static watermark such as SAMPLE can be enough and can be prepared using the free browser tool. A purchased file may use dynamic information from an order instead. Keep the preview and customer master as separate files so you do not accidentally sell the sample. After replacing a PDF, repeat the readability and delivery tests; a new page size can move the same stamp into the content.')]
}
